<title>USA: OccuSystems to be on S&amp;P SmallCap 600.</title>
<headline>OccuSystems to be on S&amp;P SmallCap 600.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Equity Services Group of Standard &amp; Poor's said Tuesday it will replace Washington Energy Co in the S&amp;P SmallCap 600 Index with OccuSystems Inc after the close of tradingon Monday, February 10.</p>
<p>Washington Energy is merging with Puget Sound Power and Light Co, a component of the S&amp;P MidCap 400 Index, to form a new company to be called Puget Sound Energy.</p>
<p>The merger is expected to close on February 10 and beginning the next day, it will be traded under the symbol. The new company will remain in the MidCap.</p>
<p>OccuSystems, which is based in Dallas, is a physician practice management company.</p>
